{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 20, :comments ["<b>you shall not go over the boughs again, you shall not glean after yourself.</b> Our Rabbis of blessed memory interpreted (Ḥullin 131a): 'after yourself' — this refers to forgetfulness. And according to the allusion, it is warning him against robbing the poor: that he should not leave his wealth to his heirs after him, in the manner that I explained regarding Lot, who was distressed over his wealth, and the angel said to him, 'do not look after yourself,' as explained in its place (Genesis 19:17). So too it says here: do not seek to adorn what will be after you, for who can tell a person what will be after him? And likewise, do not seek to leave the gleanings for whoever will be after you, but rather for the stranger, for the orphan it shall be — and then you will see your world in your lifetime. And do not worry to say: if I leave nothing at all after me, how will my children be sustained? Concerning this it says: 'and you shall remember that you were a slave in the land of Egypt' — lacking everything, for whatever a slave acquires, his master acquires; yet even so, you have now merited fields and vineyards through the will of El, blessed be He. He will also send His angel before your seed after you and give them sufficient for their needs. And therefore it is good for you to prepare for the needs of your eternal home, for a person is closer to himself than to his children after him; therefore he should not seek and demand what will be after him, in the way that most of the rich of our generation act — they make wealth but not with justice, and they are stout-hearted, far removed from charity, and they claim that they do so for the sake of their children, yet they themselves will carry nothing of their labor into the eternal world. Woe to that shame and disgrace."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :kli-yakar, :lang :en, :chapter 24, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:13:42.253019Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}